  "componentNotes": [
    {
      "title": "Pelican: a supported two-filer union",
      "text": "The company history supports the current Pelican brand across CP-Tel (130362) and Northeast Louisiana Telephone (130939). Their measured Louisiana components are 6,835 and 1,779 unique locations; the deduplicated union is 8,614. This is the union used in the summary and county export.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "PELICAN-ABOUT",
        "FCC-D25-LA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SATCO: legal filer and ARIS joint venture remain separate",
      "text": "SATCO 131214 is a legal-filer-only screen, not a certified wholly owned asset perimeter. ARIS 440163 is the separately reported OECC/SATCO joint venture. Independent raw-file review finds 57 shared locations between the two Arkansas components; their geometric union is 12,471, not 12,528, but no combined acquisition case is scored. The Louisiana SATCO file contains 3,517 business-only FTTP rows and zero R/X rows. That is a measured exclusion, not a missing file or an absent business network.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "FCC-D25-AR",
        "FCC-D25-LA",
        "OECC-ARIS",
        "AR-ARIS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dragonfly: fiber components only, with no represented buyer comparison",
      "text": "SP Broadband 410184 contributes 475 Alabama FTTP locations. Myakka 130880 contributes 4,950 Florida locations. Dragonfly says the Myakka acquisition finalized December 24, 2025; the January 2026 announcement is not the closing date. Components remain separate because the historical identities and complete current platform are not certified. Fast Wireless technology 70 and SP Broadband Florida technology 72 are excluded from this FTTP screen. Both Alabama and Florida state files were validated; the selected historical buyer filers are not represented.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "FCC-D25-AL",
        "FCC-D25-FL",
        "DRAGONFLY-MYAKKA",
        "DRAGONFLY-FAST",
        "DRAGONFLY-CURRENT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Aeneas: Tennessee is the measured component",
      "text": "This calculation includes filer 190015 in Tennessee only. Its Mississippi catalog entry lies outside the validated 21-state input set and has an unresolved current perimeter, so it is excluded rather than presumed zero. Aeneas ownership does not establish title to every cooperative network asset used to deliver service.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "FCC-D25-CATALOG",
        "FCC-D25-TN",
        "AENEAS-STEMC-1",
        "AENEAS-STEMC-2"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "method": "Five complete State / Location Coverage / Fixed Broadband technology-50 CSV files were checked against retained catalog row counts and SHA-256 hashes. The calculation filters technology 50 and residential-capable R/X, selects supported provider IDs, deduplicates location_id, and rejects conflicting county assignments. Exact overlap is the intersection of buyer and target location sets. County identity comes from the first five digits of block_geoid. Independent review reconstructed the raw-file counts and intersections separately.",
  "limits": [
    "Availability date is December 31, 2025; catalog revision is September 15, 2026. Current retail and ownership sources were checked September 20, 2026. Later builds and changed reporting are not measured here.",
    "County co-presence means both report eligible locations within the same county. It does not mean adjacent network routes, shared endpoints, construction adjacency or interconnection. No mileage or transport adjacency has been calculated.",
    "The summary compares the buyer only within each target state. County views show all counties with target locations; a buyer may have locations in additional counties not displayed there. Union is the deduplicated buyer-plus-target set in the stated geography.",
    "These seven target groups are a bounded Southern screen. PhireLink/Arkwest and other broader platforms need additional historical-filer mapping before a complete platform overlap can be claimed.",
    "Business-only service, wireless and other non-FTTP technologies are excluded. The screen therefore does not answer enterprise route overlap, carrier backhaul availability or MDU property access.",
    "No aggregate acquisition benefit is calculated by summing targets. Target-target overlap, asset rights, purchase perimeter, current operating data, capex and seller willingness require separate diligence."
  ],
